From: Local rebuild <local@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: Apply configurable V4L2 controls when the input starts

Some camera sensors need controls applied after their libcamera pipeline has
configured the device. Applying them before streaming is ineffective because
libcamera overwrites them while moving the pipeline to PLAYING.

Add a repeatable --input-start-control=DEVICE:CONTROL=VALUE option. DEVICE is
a V4L2 device path, CONTROL is either a numeric control ID or a case-insensitive
name with punctuation normalized to underscores, and VALUE is a signed integer.
Apply every configured control whenever the input pipeline reaches PLAYING.
Failures are logged independently and do not stop the video stream.
---
